there must be a corresponding `NNNNNN.ots` file.\\n\\nLet me check the test to see what behavior is expected:\\n\\n```python\\ndef test_check_anchors_requires_the_writer_to_cover_every_entry(self):\\n    # review 1: a hand-written entry passed every check. Now an entry no writer attestation covers is wrong.\\n    self._two_entries()\\n    rc, out, err = self.run_cmd(\\\"check-anchors\\\")\\n    self.assertEqual(rc, 1)\\n    self.assertIn(\\\"never attested by the writer\\\", err)\\n```\\n\\nThis test expects check-anchors to fail when there are no anchors at all (just entries).\\n\\nNow I need to add logic to check that for every sigstore anchor (which attests a range ending at `seq`), there's a corresponding `.ots` file for that same `seq`.\\n\\nLet me implement this fix. I'll track which sequences have sigstore anchors (range heads) and which have ots anchors, then verify that every sigstore range head has a corresponding ots file.\\n\\nLooking at the code again, I see that `ranges` is a list of `(from_seq, to_seq, commit)` tuples. The `to_seq` is the range head. So I need to check that for each `(from_seq, to_seq, commit)` in `ranges`, there exists a `{to_seq:06d}.ots` file in the anchors directory.\\n\\nLet me add this check after collecting all the anchors.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me understand the issue better. The `cmd_check_anchors` function processes anchor files but doesn't verify that every Sigstore-attested range head (the `to_seq` in a `.sigstore.json` file) has a corresponding `.ots` proof file. Let me add this check.\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-13da895b-b9c5-4e37-9553-cac33856da02","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/record/record.py","edits":[{"oldText":"    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit","newText":"    # Every Sigstore-attested range head (hi) must have a corresponding .ots proof file.\n    ots_seqs = {int(m.group(1)) for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\")\n                if (m := ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(os.path.basename(path))) and m.group(2) == \"ots\"}\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if hi not in ots_seqs:\n            bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":14015,"output":1476,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":880,"totalTokens":15491,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794872759447,"responseId":"gen-1794872759-CKgBx49MbK9ReEshXlWH","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":12908,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResu