{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fix looks correct. The error message format is `f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\"` which produces exactly `000002.ots is missing` for sequence 2, matching the requirement.\n\nLet me also verify that:\n1. The check happens for every successfully verified sigstore anchor (those in `ranges`)\n2. It prints to stderr with \"BAD: \" prefix (which the code does at the end with `print(f\"BAD: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)`)\n3. It exits with code 1 when there are bad entries\n\nAll looks good. Let me also make sure the test `test_check_anchors_requires_the_writer_to_cover_every_entry` still works as expected - it creates two entries with no anchors at all, so `ranges` will be empty and the new check won't trigger, but the existing check for \"entries never attested\" will still catch it.\n\nLet me also think about edge cases:\n- What if there's a sigstore anchor for range 1-2 and another for 3-4, but only 000002.ots exists (missing 000004.ots)? The check will catch both missing files correctly.\n- What if there's an .ots file but no corresponding sigstore anchor? That's fine - the requirement is only one-way (sigstore anchor → .ots must exist).\n- What if the sigstore anchor verifies but has a `to_seq` that doesn't match its filename? The code already validates `pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq` and raises Bad, so it won't be added to `ranges`.\n\nEverything looks solid. Let me run the tests one more time to confirm.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The fix looks correct. The error message format is `f\\\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\\\"` which produces exactly `000002.ots is missing` for sequence 2, matching the requirement.\\n\\nLet me also verify that:\\n1. The check happens for every successfully verified sigstore anchor (those in `ranges`)\\n2. It prints to stderr with \\\"BAD: \\\" prefix (which the code does at the end with `print(f\\\"BAD: {x}\\\", file=sys.stderr)`)\\n3. It exits with code 1 when there are bad entries\\n\\nAll looks good. Let me also make sure the test `test_check_anchors_requires_the_writer_to_cover_every_entry` still works as expected - it creates two entries with no anchors at all, so `ranges` will be empty and the new check won't trigger, but the existing check for \\\"entries never attested\\\" will still catch it.\\n\\nLet me also think about edge cases:\\n- What if there's a sigstore anchor for range 1-2 and another for 3-4, but only 000002.ots exists (missing 000004.ots)? The check will catch both missing files correctly.\\n- What if there's an .ots file but no corresponding sigstore anchor? That's fine - the requirement is only one-way (sigstore anchor → .ots must exist).\\n- What if the sigstore anchor verifies but has a `to_seq` that doesn't match its filename? The code already validates `pred.get(\\\"to_seq\\\") != seq` and raises Bad, so it won't be added to `ranges`.\\n\\nEverything looks solid. Let me run the tests one more time to confirm.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in place and the error message format matches the requirement exactly (`NNNNNN.ots is missing`). Let me run the tests one final time to confirm everything works:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-1633ea8b-946d-499a-b76c-3470663a88b8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -m unittest test_record 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":1959,"output":440,"cacheRead":21920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":364,"totalTokens":24319,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794872808264,"responseId":"gen-1794872808-s7byvY0KG2W6nmyizGT2","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":6108,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-1633ea8b-946d-499a-b76c-3470663