ning.text\",\"text\":\"All tests pass. Let me also verify the fix handles the case where there are multiple sigstore anchors correctly, and the error message format is exactly as required.\\n\\nLet me also check the exact output format by looking at how the \\\"BAD:\\\" messages are printed.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Let me verify the error message format matches the requirement exactly by checking the code:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-e39ac102-9698-4767-8848-5eb2391e0bbc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/record/record.py","offset":260,"limit":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":4007,"output":125,"cacheRead":17536,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":52,"totalTokens":21668,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794872803698,"responseId":"gen-1794872803-owXYtnwO2nIS7aL0JxsL","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":3257,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-e39ac102-9698-4767-8848-5eb2391e0bbc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    print(json.dumps({\"entries\": len(chain), \"head_seq\": len(chain), \"head_sha256\": chain[-1][1] if chain else None,\n                      \"plans\": len(plans), \"verdicts\": len(verdict_of),\n                      \"orphans_explained\": sum(e[\"kind\"] == \"orphan\" for e, _ in chain),\n                      \"open_plans\": open_, \"overdue_plans\": overdue}, indent=1))\n    return 0\n\n\ndef cmd_head(a):\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    print(f\"{len(chain)} {chain[-1][1] if chain else '-'}\")\n    return 0\n\n\n# ---------- anchors ----------\ndef _get(url, data=None, timeout=20, headers=False):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\",\n                                                          \"User-Agent\": \"exagium-record\"})\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:\n            body = r.read()\n            return (body, r.headers) if headers else body\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as ex:\n        if ex.code == 404:\n            return (None, None) if headers else None\n        raise CantCheck(f\"network: {url}: HTTP {ex.code}\")\n    except OSError as ex:\n        raise CantCheck(f\"network: {url}: {ex}\")\n\n\ndef identity(repo, workflow, ref):\n    return f\"https://github.com/{repo}/{workflow}@{ref}\"\n\n\ndef range_predicate(chain, from_seq, to_seq):\n    \"\"\"What the writer attests: the range of entries one run added, tied to the chain on both ends.\"\"\"\n    return {\"from_seq\": from_seq, \"to_seq\": to_seq,\n            \"prev_sha256\": chain[from_seq - 2][1] if from_seq > 1 else None, \"head_sha256\": chain[to_seq - 1][1]}\n\n\ndef check_sigstore(bundle, digest, repo, workflow, ref):\n    \"\"\"Verify offline that a bundle is an attestation of this digest, signed by exactly this workflow on this ref.\n    Returns (integrated_time, predicate). Wrong data is Bad; a missing library is CantCheck.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from sigstore.models import Bundle\n        from sigstore.verify import Verifier, policy\n        from sigstore.errors import Error as SigstoreError\n    except ImportError as ex:\n        raise CantCheck(f\"sigstore-python isn't usable ({ex}); pip install sigstore==4.5.1 in a virtualenv\")\n    name = os.path.basename(bundle)\n    raw = open(bundle, \"rb\").read()\n    pol = policy.AllOf([policy.Identity(identity=identity(repo, workflow, ref), issuer=ISSUER),\n                        policy.GitHubWorkflowRepository(repo), policy.GitHubWorkflowRef(ref)])\n    try:\n        b = Bundle.from_json(raw)\n        ptype, payload = Verifier.production(offline=True).verify_dsse(b, pol)\n    except SigstoreError as ex:   # verification errors and malformed bundles alike: the anchor is wrong\n        raise Bad(f\"{name}: Sigstore verification failed: {ex}\")\n    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError) as ex:\n        raise Bad(f\"{name}: malformed bundle ({type(ex).__name__}: {ex})\")\n    st = parse_json(payload, f\"{name} payload\")\n\n[318 more lines in file. Use offset=320 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":2,"timestamp":1794872806958},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me find the check_anchors function where I added the fix to verify the message format.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Let me find the check_anchors function where I added the fix to verify the message format.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2b1e5d29-b669-4c12-bf5e-0048dd2abea8","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/record/record.py","limit":80,"offset":380}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":4931,"output":74,"cacheRead":17536,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":20,"totalTokens":22541,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794872806959,"responseId":"gen-1794872806-vXZ2LaLrwevxeifohbq1","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1303,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-2b1e5d29-b669-4c12-bf5e-0048dd2abea8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    return datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(t, datetime.timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\") if t else None\n\n\ndef cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, and the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges = [], [], [], []\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})\n        except Bad as ex:\n            bad.append(str(ex))\n        except CantCheck as ex:\n            cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n    # Every Sigstore-attested range head (hi) must have a corresponding .ots proof file.\n    ots_seqs = {int(m.group(1)) for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\")\n                if (m := ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(os.path.basename(path))) and m.group(2) == \"ots\"}\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if hi not in ots_seqs:\n            bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")\n    print(json.dumps({\"anchors\": rows, \"entries\": len(chain), \"writer_attested_through\": covered,\n                      \"writer_runs\": changes, \"wrong\": bad, \"could_not_check\": cant}, indent=1))\n    for x in bad:\n        print(f\"BAD: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    for x in cant:\n        print(f\"CAN'T CHECK: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    return 1 if bad else 2 if cant else 0\n\n\ndef _git(a, *args):\n    root = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(a.ledger))\n    r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", root, *args], capture_output=True)\n    return r.stdout if r.returncode == 0 else None\n\n\ndef _code_changed(a, c1, c2):\n    \"\"\"True/False if anything under record/ or .github/ differs between two commits; \"unknown\" without that history.\"\"\"\n    if _git(a, \"cat-file\", \"-e\", f\"{c1}^{{commit}}\") is None or _git(a, \"cat-file\", \"-e\", f\"{c2}^{{commit}}\") is None:\n        return \"unknown (commit not in this clone)\"\n    root = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(a.ledger))\n    r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", root, \"diff\", \"--quiet\", c1, c2, \"--\", \"record\", \".github\"])\n    return {0: False, 1: True}.get(r.returncode, \"unknown\")\n\n\ndef _orphan_entries_problem(o, pred):\n    \"\"\"The orphan must publish the hidden entries: canonical, consecutive from from_seq, chained from prev_sha256,\n    ending at head_sha256. Returns a description of the first problem, or None.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        raws = [base64.b64decode(x) for x in o[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]]\n        if not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or len(raws) != pred.get(\"to_seq\", -1) - pred[\"from_seq\"] + 1:\n            return \"its entries don't match the attested range\"\n        prev = pred.get(\"prev_sha256\")\n\n[178 more lines in file. Use offset=460 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":1,"timestamp":1794872808263},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fix looks correct. The error message format is `f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\"` which produces exactly `000002.ots is missing` for sequence 2, matching the requirement.\n\nLet me also verify that:\n1. The check happens for every successfully verified sigstore anchor (those in `ranges`)\n2. It prints to stderr with \"BAD: \" prefix (which the code does at the end with `print(f\"BAD: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)`)\n3. It exits with code 1 when there are bad entries\n\nAll looks good. Let me also make sure the test `test_check_anchors_requires_the_writer_to_cover_every_entry` still works as expected - it creates two entries with no anchors at all, so `ranges` will be empty and the new check won't trigger, but the existing check for \"entries never attested\" will still catch it.\n\nLet me also think about edge cases:\n- What if there's a sigstore anchor for range 1-2 and another for 3-4, but only 000002.ots exists (missing 000004.ots)? The check will catch both missing files correctly.\n- What if there's an .ots file but no corresponding sigstore anchor? That's fine - the requirement is only one-way (sigstore anchor → .ots must exist).\n- What if the sigstore anchor verifies but has a `to_seq` that doesn't match its filename? The code already validates `pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq` and raises Bad, so it won't be added to `ranges`.\n\nEverything looks solid. Let me run the tests one more time to confirm.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The fix looks correct. The error message format is `f\\\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\\\"` which produces exactly `000002.ots is missing` for sequence 2, matching the requirement.\\n\\nLet me also verify that:\\n1. The check happens for every successfully verified sigstore anchor (those in `ranges`)\\n2. It prints to stderr with \\\"BAD: \\\" prefix (which the code does at the end with `print(f\\\"BAD: {x}\\\", file=sys.stderr)`)\\n3. It exits with code 1 when there are bad entries\\n\\nAll looks good. Let me also make sure the test `test_check_anchors_requires_the_writer_to_cover_every_entry` still works as expected - it creates two entries with no anchors at all, so `ranges` will be empty and the new check won't trigger, but the existing check for \\\"entries never attested\\\" will still catch it.\\n\\nLet me also think about edge cases:\\n- What if there's a sigstore anchor for range 1-2 and another for 3-4, but only 000002.ots exists (missing 000004.ots)? The check will catch both missing files correctly.\\n- What if there's an .ots file but no corresponding sigstore anchor? That's fine - the requirement is only one-way (sigstore anchor → .ots must exist).\\n- What if the sigstore anchor verifies but has a `to_seq` that doesn't match its filename? The code already validates `pred.get(\\\"to_seq\\\") != seq` and raises Bad, so it won't be added to `ranges`.\\n\\nEverything looks solid. Let me run the tests one more time to confirm.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in place and the error message format matches the requirement exactly (`NNNNNN.ots is missing`). Let me run the tests one final time to confirm everything works:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-1633ea8b-946d-499a-b76c-3470663a88b8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -m unittest test_record 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"